-- title:
--   Kernel vanishes near a smooth point with no cotangent-rank drop
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $B$ be a $k$-algebra of finite type which is smooth over $k$ (in Mathlib's sense: formally smooth and of finite presentation), let $B'$ be a commutative $k$-algebra, and let $\psi : B \to B'$ be a surjective $k$-algebra homomorphism. Let $v'$ be a prime ideal of $B'$ and $v$ a prime ideal of $B$ with $v = \psi^{-1}(v')$. Assume that $B'$ is smooth over $k$ at $v'$, i.e. the local ring $B'_{v'}$ is formally smooth over $k$, and assume the cotangent fibre does not drop: $$\dim_{\kappa(v)}\bigl(\kappa(v)\otimes_B \Omega^1_{B/k}\bigr) \le \dim_{\kappa(v')}\bigl(\kappa(v')\otimes_{B'} \Omega^1_{B'/k}\bigr),$$ where $\kappa(v)$ and $\kappa(v')$ denote the residue fields of the respective primes and the dimensions are module ranks over those fields. The conclusion is that there exists $t \in B$ with $t \notin v$ such that the ideal of the localisation $B_t =$ `Localization.Away t` generated by the image of $\ker \psi$ under $B \to B_t$ is the zero ideal; equivalently, $\ker\psi$ dies after inverting $t$.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a closed subscheme of a smooth $k$-scheme, presented by an arbitrary surjection of $k$-algebras, coincides with the ambient scheme on a neighbourhood of a point at which it is smooth with cotangent fibre of the same dimension. It feeds into [`Algebra.exists_smooth_surjective_localizationAway_basis_kaehlerDifferential_comap_eq_span`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_smooth_surjective_localizationAway_basis_kaehlerDifferential_comap_eq_span), which produces a smooth localisation together with a basis of its module of Kähler differentials.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_exists_notMem_map_ker_eq_bot_of_surjective_of_isSmoothAt_of_finrank_le.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open TensorProduct KaehlerDifferential

universe u

theorem Algebra.exists_notMem_map_ker_eq_bot_of_surjective_of_isSmoothAt_of_finrank_le
    {k : Type u} [Field k] {B : Type u} [CommRing B] [Algebra k B] [Algebra.FiniteType k B] [Algebra.Smooth k B]
    {B' : Type u} [CommRing B'] [Algebra k B'] (ψ : B →ₐ[k] B') (hψ : Function.Surjective ψ)
    (v' : Ideal B') [v'.IsPrime] (v : Ideal B) [v.IsPrime] (hv' : v'.comap ψ.toRingHom = v)
    (hsm : Algebra.IsSmoothAt k v')
    (hrank : Module.finrank v.ResidueField (v.ResidueField ⊗[B] Ω[B⁄k]) ≤
      Module.finrank v'.ResidueField (v'.ResidueField ⊗[B'] Ω[B'⁄k])) :
    ∃ t : B, t ∉ v ∧ (RingHom.ker ψ.toRingHom).map (algebraMap B (Localization.Away t)) = ⊥ := by sorry
